// Title: Malicious DLL File Dropped in the Teams or OneDrive Folder
// Sigma ID: 1908fcc1-1b92-4272-8214-0fbaf2fa5163
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-08-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects creation of a malicious DLL file in the location where the OneDrive or Team applications
//   Upon execution of the Teams or OneDrive application, the dropped malicious DLL file
//   ("iphlpapi.dll") is sideloaded
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.cyble.com/2022/07/27/targeted-attacks-being-carried-out-via-dll-sideloading/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_iphlpapi_dll_sideloading.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "iphlpapi.dll" and FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft"
